Enable WebKit's native picture in picture, and add a button for it.

WebKit only enables the context menu's "Enter Picture in Picture" when
Settings::allowsPictureInPictureMediaPlayback is on (ContextMenuController
sets shouldEnable from HitTestResult::mediaSupportsPictureInPicture, which
reaches MediaElementSession::allowsPictureInPicture). For WKWebView on macOS
that setting defaults to false, so the item is appended for the video and then
drawn disabled.

With the setting on, webkitSetPresentationMode also starts working, so the
watch view gets a button over the top-right corner of the video that hands
playback to the system window. It fades in on hover, the way the system's own
picture in picture window reveals its controls. Leaving is handled by that
window's restore control, so there is no exit path here.

This is deliberately not wired to the existing player bar picture in picture
button, which pops out to Kaset's own floating NSWindow. Upstream would
probably want the two behind a preference rather than side by side.

diff -ru a/Sources/Kaset/Services/WebKit/WebKitManager.swift b/Sources/Kaset/Services/WebKit/WebKitManager.swift
